==================================================================
 PART 1 — the default: one cause is assumed, silently
==================================================================

  The watched cell is Northeast / Outdoor and it is broken in all
  four runs, identically. `others` counts how many UNRELATED cells
  are broken at the same time.

  others  watched change   pop. mean   pop. sd      z   verdict
  ------  --------------   ---------   -------   ----   -------
  0       -25728           -666        6974      -5.7   FOUND
  1       -25728           -1643       8472      -3.65   FOUND
  2       -25728           -2663       9668      -2.83   nothing
  4       -25728           -4942       12213     -1.86   nothing

  The watched cell never changed. The population around it did, and
  that is enough to take it from a finding to nothing at all.

==================================================================
 PART 2 — allowing for more than one
==================================================================

  `max_causes` excludes the other candidates from the REFERENCE. It
  does not bless them as findings; it declines to let them define
  what ordinary looks like. The permuted null is required, because
  trimming changes the statistic and the t formula is a formula for
  the untrimmed one.

  others  max_causes   watched z   threshold   verdict
  ------  ----------   ---------   ---------   -------
  1       2            -5.59       4.35        FOUND
  2       3            -5.46       4.84        FOUND
  4       5            -5.48       6.46        nothing

  The bar rises with what you allow for. That is the trade and it
  cannot be avoided: a population that may contain five broken cells
  is a population in which any one of them is less surprising.

==================================================================
 PART 3 — the refusal
==================================================================

  insight.explain_change: max_causes above 1 needs null: "siblings_permuted" -- trimming the reference changes the statistic, and the t threshold is a formula for the untrimmed one. The permuted null takes its threshold from the statistic actually used, so it follows the trim; the t formula does not and would report causes that are not there

==================================================================
 WHAT THIS MEASURED
==================================================================

  1. THE TEST FINDS A PROBLEM ONLY WHILE IT IS NEARLY THE ONLY
     PROBLEM. Four unrelated cells collapsing beside the watched one
     halve its z and take it below the bar, without one number in
     that cell changing. Both terms of the standardisation move at
     once: the reference mean slides towards the anomaly and the
     reference spread inflates.

  2. TWO OBVIOUS REPAIRS WERE MEASURED AND BOTH FAILED. Sequential
     peeling -- test the most extreme, remove it, test the next --
     does not help, because the FIRST test is the most contaminated
     and it is the one that decides whether anything is reported.
     A robust median/MAD scale does not help either: at 24 cells the
     MAD itself rose 28% between one cause and two, and once its own
     null threshold is measured honestly (4.18, against the t
     formula's 3.49) the robust statistic is FURTHER from clearing.

  3. WHAT WORKS IS A DECLARED CHOICE, NOT A BETTER DEFAULT.
     Excluding the other candidates from the reference restores the
     statistic to a property of the cell: the trimmed z sits at
     -5.5 in all three runs, where the default fell from -3.65 to
     -1.86. But the bar rises with what is allowed for -- 4.35,
     4.84, 6.46 -- and by five causes in twenty-four cells it has
     outrun the evidence. That third row is the honest half: this
     is a trade with a limit, not a repair.

  4. SO THE NUMBER OF THINGS THAT MAY BE WRONG AT ONCE IS THE
     CALLER'S TO STATE, like the null and the comparison. Its
     default of 1 is not a new assumption -- it is the one that was
     always being made, now written down where it can be argued
     with, and recorded in the Finding as `search.max_causes`.
